INT. RIDESHARE CAR - NIGHT

JAMAL (V.O.)
Two a.m. Wet road. Empty streets. Nothing on the radio but static.

JAMAL
(eyes in the mirror, thumb tapping the wheel)
Five stars is all I ask, folks. Everyone buckled?

COLE
(slumped against the window, fogging the glass)
Yeah, Jamal. Drive.

JAMAL (V.O.)
Four kids from a party. Three of them quiet. One of them loud. Always one.

RUBEN
(leaning forward between the seats, grinning)
Cole, tell him what you did. Tell Jamal what you did at Tasha's.

COLE
(shoving Ruben's face away)
Shut up Ruben.

BIANCA
(arms folded, not looking at either boy)
He told her he loved her. Then he threw up in her mom's plant.

SHAY
(whispering, holding a phone dark in her lap)
Bianca. Stop.

JAMAL (V.O.)
Red light. Rain. Nobody talks. The wipers keep time.

MIKA
(from the front passenger seat, finally, softly)
Jamal, can you drop me first? Please. He said he'd call and he's not going to, and I don't want him to see me cry.

JAMAL
(gently, to Mika)
Sure thing. Anywhere you like.

COLE
(to Shay, low)
He means me, right?

SHAY
(not unkindly)
He means the other he, Cole.
